```xml
<RefreshView IsRefreshing="{Binding IsRefreshing, Mode=TwoWay}"
             Command="{Binding RefreshCommand}">
    <CollectionView ItemsSource="{Binding Results}"
                    SelectionMode="Single"
                    SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedResult, Mode=TwoWay}">
        <CollectionView.ItemTemplate>
            <DataTemplate x:DataType="models:SearchResult">
                <Label Text="{Binding Title}" Padding="8" />
            </DataTemplate>
        </CollectionView.ItemTemplate>
    </CollectionView>
</RefreshView>
```

`SelectedResult` now receives the selected object in the view model. The refresh command must clear the busy state even when reload fails:

```csharp
public ObservableCollection<SearchResult> Results { get; } = [];
public SearchResult? SelectedResult { get; set; }
public bool IsRefreshing { get; set; }

private async Task RefreshAsync()
{
    try
    {
        IsRefreshing = true;
        var latest = await api.GetResultsAsync();
        Results.Clear();
        foreach (var item in latest)
            Results.Add(item);
    }
    finally
    {
        IsRefreshing = false;
    }
}
```

`RefreshCommand` should invoke `RefreshAsync` and the properties should raise change notifications.
